      "writtenOn": "2026-09-29T11:53:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The most expensive part of this API call is opening the repository.\nSince `All-Users.git` will always exist and never be deleted or renamed, can we just open the repository and keep it open here?",
      "revId": "f2f8c01e21ad6f5375ac2e19c80c22441fbde7da",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "83cda2d6_f882acb3",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/server/account/AuthTokenCache.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 79,
      "author": {
        "id": 1072905
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-29T16:30:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`openRepository` already returns a cached handle, though, right?\n\n```\nreturn RepositoryCache.open(...);\n```\n\nThe [AccountCache](https://gerrit.googlesource.com/gerrit/+/refs/heads/master/java/com/google/gerrit/server/account/AccountCacheImpl.java#159) does the same.\n\nIf we kept it open, we would hold a resource handle for the entire lifetime of the cache.\n\nWDYT?",
      "parentUuid": "83705e41_068090ca",
      "revId": "f2f8c01e21ad6f5375ac2e19c80c22441fbde7da",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "daf50d89_2265ff53",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/server/account/AuthTokenCache.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 79,
      "author": {
        "id": 1006192
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-29T17:15:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The `LocalDiskRepositoryManager.openRepository` does:\n\n```\n    if (isUnreasonableName(name)) {\n      throw new RepositoryNotFoundException(\"Invalid name: \" + name);\n    }\n    FileKey location \u003d\n        usePerRequestRefCache\n            ? DynamicRefDbRepository.FileKey.lenient(\n                getBasePath(name).resolve(name.get()).toFile(),\n                FS.DETECTED,\n                (path, refDb) -\u003e PerThreadRefDbCache.getRefDatabase(path, refDb))\n            : FileKey.lenient(getBasePath(name).resolve(name.get()).toFile(), FS.DETECTED);\n    try {\n      Repository repo \u003d RepositoryCache.open(location);\n      if (useFileKeyByProjectCache) {\n        fileKeyByProject.put(name, location);\n      }\n      return repo;\n    } catch (IOException e) {\n      throw new RepositoryNotFoundException(\"Cannot open repository \" + name, e);\n    }\n```\n\nSpecifically, calculating the `FileKey location` may take tens to hundreds of milliseconds.\n\nThis API is used in the call stack of an HTTP authentication call, which could be used by robots quite intensively.\n\n\u003e If we kept it open, we would hold a resource handle for the entire lifetime of the cache.\n\nI am pretty sure that the resource handle is *always used* in Gerrit when the JVM is on: I cannot imagine a Gerrit JVM running and serving requests without having the `All-Users.git` repository open and in cache.",
      "parentUuid": "83cda2d6_f882acb3",
      "revId": "f2f8c01e21ad6f5375ac2e19c80c22441fbde7da",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
